1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,071
Welcome to Color Practice!

2
00:00:02,071 --> 00:00:05,098
Let's play with paint and see what we can discover.

3
00:00:05,098 --> 00:00:08,970
Start with red, yellow, blue, black, and white.

4
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:11,323
A little paint can take you a long way!

5
00:00:11,323 --> 00:00:13,431
Watch how real paint behaves.

6
00:00:13,431 --> 00:00:16,151
Try a little more water, or a little more color.

7
00:00:16,151 --> 00:00:18,224
Mix, paint, and compare.

8
00:00:18,224 --> 00:00:21,813
Change the amounts, and watch a whole new color appear!

9
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,399
Save your discoveries in your own palette.

10
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:26,899
You're learning to notice tiny differences.

11
00:00:26,899 --> 00:00:29,106
Next, explore Color Neighbors.

12
00:00:29,106 --> 00:00:33,823
Use lighter and darker colors to make simple shapes feel round and solid.

13
00:00:33,823 --> 00:00:36,102
Then try Complementary Colors.

14
00:00:36,102 --> 00:00:40,465
Discover how opposite colors help you paint shadows and reflected light.

15
00:00:40,465 --> 00:00:42,046
No need to get it perfect.

16
00:00:42,046 --> 00:00:45,232
Try something, be curious, and have fun!

17
00:00:45,232 --> 00:00:46,495
Let's start mixing.

